refused (cp-isk-seed-public): isk.txt says "seed public". cp_commit writes that line only with -public-weights, and such a commitment hides nothing. To serve it, give -public-weights with the file that it was created with. If you created this commitment without that option, someone else writes into isk. Then do not remove the line: switch off whatever restarts cp_prove, the model server and whatever calls cp_commit by itself, then stop every cp_prove on this isk and wait until each has ended, make no further call of cp_commit or cp_prove on it, and go by docs/operators-duties.md, "If the count is lost or in doubt", before anything else
